\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Cutting the grid}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{On a periodic grid, a forward step from the last layer reaches
the first. Removing this step and its reverse leaves two faces.
A field confined to one of them can still produce a value on its
neighbor under the [Wilson operator](fdip-009U). Which part of a
spin field does that hop see? When the neighboring value vanishes,
what condition remains on the face itself?}
